{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And I lifted my eyes and saw</b> — In night visions, like the way of Zechariah the prophet. Know that their rank is greater than the rank of Gideon and Manoah and his wife, and the discerning will understand. <b>Of gold of Uphaz</b> — The alef is superfluous, like the alef in אתמול and אזרוע and אשמור." "<b>And bolt</b> — It is round, containing pure gold."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The alef in אופז is taken as superfluous relative to פז (pure gold); the three Hebrew forms cited illustrate other words where an alef is similarly added."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:50.760637113Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}